WEBVTT

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.900
Indeed, humans are sinful and foolish.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.740
Indeed, humans are sinful and foolish.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.740
That's what I 
like about us.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.740
That's what I like about us.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.740
<b>Episode 15</b>

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.740
<b>Dazai-san's 
Nail Biter</b>

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.250
Wh-What...

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.000
Dazai!

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.460
Who told you to make origami 
out of our documents?!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.250
<b>Daily Report</b>

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.250
<b>Today was a nice
 and uneventful day.</b>

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.250
And what is this report?!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.840
Do it over!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:30.960
Here.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.630
Don't toss your job aside!

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.380
Do your work properly for once!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.680
Sheesh, Kunikida-kun's always so angry.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.350
Some people never learn.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.810
I know, right? What do we do with that man?

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.890
What do we do?

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.060
I'm talking about you!

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.730
You should stop slacking.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.150
A day without messing with Kunikida-kun

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:52.650
<b>Sad</b>

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.190
is like a fizzy drink without its fizz 
or a rice cracker without its crunch.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.650
You have to close your containers.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.240
Kunikida-kun's indignation 
is the spice of life.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.280
Nah, the seasoning.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.530
Like green onions!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.330
Kunikida is green onion.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.490
You're more like ginger.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.040
<b>Spice Boys</b>

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.290
Kunikida-kun!

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.290
What?

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.290
Oh, nothing.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.210
I see you're hard at work.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.170
<b>I don't know how to lie</b>

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.170
<b>I am an honest person</b>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.170
<i>There, got him.</i>

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.840
<i>Operation Advertise-Kunikida-kun's-
Good-Qualities commences.</i>

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.220
What the hell is this?!

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.510
<i>I'll never understand you.</i>

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.350
Hey, where did Kunikida-kun go?

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.020
I heard the boss has a private meeting with 
some government figures or something.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.190
Super-top-secret, sensitive information.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.400
He could only bring along 
people he trusts intimately.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:36.400
Aw, I guess I won't have a 
chance to check on him, then.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.700
<i>I might have done something 
really, really bad.</i>

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.990
Let's call it a day.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.620
Please be careful not divulge any details.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.200
Indeed.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:45.910
Rest assured, we will not.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:51.840
<b>I don't know how to lie</b>

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:51.840
<b>I am an honest human being</b>

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.330
Wait! What is that sheet of paper?

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.840
We need you to keep the secret, 
even if you have to lie!

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:52.840
<b>Clang!</b>

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.550
Wait! please!

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.430
Oh-Oh-Oh, no!

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.260
Kunikida-kun's going to be 
forced to eat bad food!

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:02.720
Huh?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.060
I have to go!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.060
<b>Conserve Energy!</b>

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.100
You don't see Dazai-san panicking 
like that very often.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:08.850
Yeah.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.190
There he is! I made it!

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.280
How can you not notice, 
though, Kunikida-kun?

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.650
The boss, too, for that matter.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.450
I am an honest human being

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.410
<i>The page curled and now it 
says something different.</i>

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.990
<i>This might be good enough.</i>

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.080
<b>I am an honest 
human being</b>

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:24.950
Wait! What is that paper?

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.040
You can't always be honest!

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:27.830
<b>Clang!</b>

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.750
This can't be!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.710
<i>That won't do.</i>

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.000
<i>It's another bad ending.</i>

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.290
<i>And it was faster than last time, too.</i>

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.720
I am a human being

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.720
<i>Now it's just a confession of his humanity!</i>

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.220
What is that paper?!

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.800
"I am a human being"? Indeed, you are.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.220
Can't blame you for being human. 
You're human, after all.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.680
All human beings are created equal.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.730
<i>That'll do.</i>

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.310
Whew, what a relief.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.310
Let's go home.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.190
Why did you go charging out earlier?

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.570
I couldn't take my eyes off the green onion.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.450
Dazai!

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.860
This was your doing, wasn't it?

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.880
<b>For more inform-ass-ion 
on the Armed Detective Agency, 
please call XXX-XXXX-XXX</b>

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.740
I made it an ad for the 
Detective Agency this time.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.500
A Hundred Tales is a classic game in 
which a hundred candles are lit,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:16.590
and they are blown out one by one after 
each of a hundred horror stories.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.930
When the last candle is snuffed out, 
something terrible is said to happen.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:23.840
So we have...

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.390
The Armed Detective Agency Hundred Tales!

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.390
<b>Episode 16</b>

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.390
<b>If Only I Could Express 
My Hundred Thoughts</b>

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.940
I object.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.150
Why should we be doing this?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.230
It's to cool us off.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.520
It's still really hot, after all.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.860
What? Are you scared, Kunikida-kun?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.070
Of course not!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.990
All right, I'll kick off our 
so-called horror stories.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.660
Woo! Yay!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.370
I had a fever that day.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.870
I remember my chills just wouldn't go away,

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.500
but I was in the middle of work.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.670
I had no choice but to 
carry on, at least until

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.250
I had finished the work in front of me.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.880
My eyes are blurry from my fever...

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.170
That's when it happened.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.220
I want to go home!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.600
I want to go to bed!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.010
The thought overtook me.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.390
Petrifying, is it not?

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.190
That's it?!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.860
I tried to abandon my plans and go home!

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.240
Me, Kunikida Doppo!

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.700
That's because you weren't feeling well!

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.450
You're no good at this, Kunikida-kun.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.910
This happened in my own room just recently.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.910
It was morning. I was supposed 
to be out of bed by that time.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.040
Something was making my head 
heavy. It was pounding.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.840
I felt sick, but I had to go to work.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.550
I did my best to get dressed and headed 
out to the Agency Headquarters.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.720
Hey! Good morning—

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.680
And that was when...

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.680
I woke up.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.680
What part of that was a horror story?!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.770
I thought I'd finally made it to the Agency,
 but I was still in bed.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.890
I had to get up and go to work again.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.520
It was so tedious—I mean, terrifying.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.690
That's just a sleepy-head problem!

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.610
You keep coming in late 
because you're so lazy!

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.820
I'm not lazy, I'm scary.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.280
What about you, Kyouka-chan?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.200
Any scary stories?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.070
Nice.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.080
Girls your age like scary stories, right?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.120
Do you have something?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.910
Um...

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.250
I was organizing documents one day.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:19.290
I remember it being sturdy, 
high quality paper.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.960
I'd gotten it between my nail and finger.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.090
I didn't notice, and I...

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.970
swiped it hard.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.470
<b>Shudder!!</b>

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.430
Also, the meat in the stew 
I had the other day was hard.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.810
It was my tongue.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.440
Wait a second!

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.020
Those aren't horror stories!

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.150
My heart's pounding just hearing about it.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.150
Hey, do you have anything, Atsushi-kun?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:44.490
M-Me?

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.950
It's not really a great story, but...

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.030
I was being punished at the orphanage.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.950
I was locked in a storage room.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.250
I noticed someone staring at me
 from behind some shelves.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.590
Does it amuse you to see me being punished?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.260
He continued staring at me.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.800
That's when I noticed...

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:14.770
There was no space beyond the 
shelves for a person to fit.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.770
What... are you?

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:22.110
Psych!

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.610
Okay, let's move on!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.280
That was the scariest one yet, Atsushi-kun.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.580
Go! Go! Go!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.540
Dazai-san's finally lost it.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:42.710
Go! Go! Gotchi go!

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.710
<b>Episode 17</b>

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.710
<b>Please Share! 
Armed Detective Agency!</b>

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.840
A dance contest?

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.340
You just have to dance 
to music and send it in.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.510
There's a cash prize for the winner.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.970
Ten-million yen?!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.470
That's amazing!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.350
I know!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.980
Why don't you join me?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:58.600
Me?!

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.350
No way!

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.350
We'd be unstoppable together, Atsushi-kun.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.980
Think of the torrent of accolades.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.400
The giant cash prize!

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.360
Cash prize?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.740
You'd be popular!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.910
I'm in!

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.710
Come on, Kunikida-kun!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.460
Join in casually, 
like you've been possessed!

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.790
It's fun!

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:26.960
Back to work.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.260
I wish you would call me out!

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.920
Oh, this is reality?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.010
A dance contest?

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:33.720
Yeah.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.350
Join us, Kunikida-kun.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.850
Why should I join?

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.020
There's a ten-million-yen cash prize.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:43.020
Our budget's been pretty slim 
as of late, hasn't it?

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:50.240
<b>Ten-million</b>

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.150
You aren't wrong.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:47.270
We could get some advertising 
done if we become famous, too.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.440
B-But...

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.240
<b>Advertising</b>

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.240
Whispers of the devil.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:51.740
Hup! Hup!

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:52.740
Three! Four!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.950
Hup! Hup!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.950
Seven! Eight!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:55.910
Bam!

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.370
No! You're so stiff, Kunikida-san!

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.370
I'm raising and lowering 
my arms, like you asked.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.920
That's your idea of choreography?!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.080
It looked like you were 
doing radio exercises!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.500
Kunikida-kun...

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:07.750
It's all right.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.380
Let's get this done right!

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.880
<b>Armed Detective
 Agency</b>

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.310
I'm back.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.820
<i>Set your heavy foot forward</i>

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.830
<i>Whatever may be the strength guiding you</i>

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.700
<i>Go ahead and ask</i>

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:46.420
<i>The impulse within you is your treasure</i>

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:52.420
<i>Whether it's real or fake, take it with you</i>

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:57.890
<i>Beyond the fantasies, I go lethargically</i>

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:02.930
<i>You can take it if you want, 
even if it's a dream</i>

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:08.610
<i>You just can't seem to reach, make some noise</i>

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:15.150
<i>Your empty lives take on light</i>

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:20.280
<i>Row forward and forward as 
though you're pushing out</i>

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:25.330
<i>And so our future catches the wind</i>

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.750
<i>Even if this moment is frozen</i>

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:34.010
<i>You can't stop me from breathing</i>

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.010
<i>It's a waste of time</i>

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:39.840
<i>Where's the prize?</i>

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.310
Hey.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.980
Welcome back.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.170
Oh, we were just...

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:53.450
You were recording a video for the
 ten-million-yen dance competition prize, right?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.740
You're right.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:55.670
Don't worry.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.420
You're definitely going to win.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:58.820
Yes!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.970
<b>Fame</b>

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.970
<b>Cash prize</b>

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.970
<b>Popularity</b>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.220
We're going to get first prize!

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:01.980
<i>A few days later...</i>

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:28.600
<b>Weirdly Unique 
Performance Prize</b>

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:28.600
<b>Armed Detective Agency</b>

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:05.860
<i>The trio won a mildly impressive prize.</i>

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:06.400
We w—

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.400
W—

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.630
Won?

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.020
<b>Prize: 3,000 yen 
gift certificate</b>

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.550
Er... Uh... Well... See...

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.300
Come on! Say something!
